          "role": "assistant",
          "text": "Yes, I am confident in the high-risk assessment for the job posting. \n\nThe primary red flag is the domain `webgocompanyy.com`, which includes an extra \"y\" at the end of \"company\". Scammers frequently register slightly misspelled domain names (a tactic known as typosquatting) to pretend to be real organizations and collect sensitive personal data from job applicants' CVs.\n\nIf you believe the hiring offer might be genuine, it is safest to look up the official company website directly through a search engine or verify their open positions on their official LinkedIn page.",
